<section class="section alt topic" id="unit1">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-title">
<div class="eyebrow">Unit 1 · 8 Periods</div>
<h2>Units and Dimensions / मात्रक एवं विमाएँ</h2>
<p>Measurement, SI system, dimensions, dimensional analysis, errors and significant figures.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">1.1</div>
<div>
<h3>Need of Measurement in Engineering and Science</h3>
<p>Engineering में measurement की आवश्यकता और units की basic understanding.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="two-lang">
<div class="english">
<h4>English Explanation</h4>
<p>Measurement is the process of comparing an unknown physical quantity with an accepted standard. Engineering design, manufacturing, testing and quality control require reliable measurements.</p>
<p>A numerical value without a unit is incomplete. For example, saying that a rod is 5 does not communicate whether the length is 5 m, 5 cm or 5 mm.</p>
</div>
<div class="hindi">
<h4>हिन्दी Explanation</h4>
<p>Measurement वह process है जिसमें किसी unknown physical quantity की तुलना किसी accepted standard से की जाती है। Engineering design, manufacturing, testing और quality control में accurate measurement आवश्यक है।</p>
<p>किसी numerical value के साथ unit होना जरूरी है। जैसे rod की length केवल 5 बताना incomplete है; 5 m, 5 cm या 5 mm स्पष्ट करना आवश्यक है।</p>
</div>
</div>

<h4>Fundamental and Derived Units / मूल एवं व्युत्पन्न मात्रक</h4>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<thead>
<tr><th>Quantity / राशि</th><th>SI Unit</th><th>Symbol</th><th>Type</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Length / लंबाई</td><td>metre</td><td>m</td><td>Fundamental</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mass / द्रव्यमान</td><td>kilogram</td><td>kg</td><td>Fundamental</td></tr>
<tr><td>Time / समय</td><td>second</td><td>s</td><td>Fundamental</td></tr>
<tr><td>Electric current</td><td>ampere</td><td>A</td><td>Fundamental</td></tr>
<tr><td>Temperature</td><td>kelvin</td><td>K</td><td>Fundamental</td></tr>
<tr><td>Amount of substance</td><td>mole</td><td>mol</td><td>Fundamental</td></tr>
<tr><td>Luminous intensity</td><td>candela</td><td>cd</td><td>Fundamental</td></tr>
<tr><td>Velocity / वेग</td><td>m/s</td><td>m s⁻¹</td><td>Derived</td></tr>
<tr><td>Force / बल</td><td>newton</td><td>N</td><td>Derived</td></tr>
<tr><td>Energy / ऊर्जा</td><td>joule</td><td>J</td><td>Derived</td></tr>
<tr><td>Power / शक्ति</td><td>watt</td><td>W</td><td>Derived</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>

<div class="note"><b>Exam Point:</b> SI system में seven base quantities होती हैं। Derived units इन्हीं base units से बनती हैं।</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">1.2</div>
<div>
<h3>Dimensions and Dimensional Formulae</h3>
<p>Physical quantities को M, L, T आदि fundamental dimensions के रूप में represent करना।</p>
</div>
</div>

<p><span class="term">Dimension:</span> किसी physical quantity को fundamental quantities की powers के रूप में express करने को dimension कहते हैं।</p>

<div class="formula">
Velocity = displacement / time<br>
[v] = [L T⁻¹]<br><br>
Acceleration = velocity / time<br>
[a] = [L T⁻²]<br><br>
Force = mass × acceleration<br>
[F] = [M L T⁻²]<br><br>
Work = force × displacement<br>
[W] = [M L² T⁻²]<br><br>
Power = work / time<br>
[P] = [M L² T⁻³]
</div>

<div class="two-lang">
<div>
<h4>English</h4>
<p>The dimensional formula indicates how a physical quantity depends on fundamental dimensions such as mass, length and time.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h4>हिन्दी</h4>
<p>Dimensional formula यह बताता है कि कोई physical quantity mass, length और time जैसी fundamental quantities पर किस power के रूप में depend करती है।</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">1.3</div>
<div>
<h3>Principle of Homogeneity of Dimensions</h3>
<p>Physical equation के दोनों sides की dimensions समान होनी चाहिए।</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
Example:<br>
s = ut + 1/2 at²<br>
[s] = L<br>
[ut] = (L T⁻¹)(T) = L<br>
[at²] = (L T⁻²)(T²) = L<br>
Therefore equation is dimensionally homogeneous.
</div>

<p class="hindi">यदि equation के किसी term की dimensions बाकी terms से अलग हो, तो equation dimensional point of view से गलत है।</p>

<div class="diagram">
<div class="diagram-title">Dimensional Homogeneity Diagram</div>
<svg viewBox="0 0 900 250" role="img" aria-label="Dimensional homogeneity diagram">
<defs>
<marker id="arrow1" markerWidth="10" markerHeight="10" refX="9" refY="3" orient="auto">
<path d="M0,0 L10,3 L0,6 Z" fill="#2458ad"></path>
</marker>
</defs>
<rect x="40" y="65" width="220" height="110" rx="18" fill="#eef5ff" stroke="#2458ad" stroke-width="3"/>
