</svg>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">1.4</div>
<div>
<h3>Dimensional Equations and Applications</h3>
<p>Unit conversion, equation checking और relation derivation.</p>
</div>
</div>

<h4>Applications / उपयोग</h4>
<ol>
<li>Checking correctness of physical equations.</li>
<li>Deriving relation between physical quantities.</li>
<li>Converting numerical values from one system of units to another.</li>
<li>Finding dimensions of constants.</li>
</ol>

<div class="formula">
General relation:<br>
Q = k Aᵃ Bᵇ Cᶜ<br>
Taking dimensions:<br>
[Q] = [A]ᵃ [B]ᵇ [C]ᶜ
</div>

<div class="warning"><b>Limitation:</b> Dimensional analysis cannot determine numerical dimensionless constants such as 2, 1/2, π and sometimes cannot distinguish quantities having identical dimensions.</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">1.5</div>
<div>
<h3>Limitations of Dimensional Analysis</h3>
<p>Dimensional method powerful है, लेकिन हर equation derive नहीं कर सकती।</p>
</div>
</div>
<ul>
<li>Dimensionless constants cannot be determined.</li>
<li>Trigonometric, exponential and logarithmic functions cannot generally be obtained from dimensions alone.</li>
<li>Different quantities may have same dimensions, for example work and torque.</li>
<li>Exact form of a relation may remain undetermined if several variables have the same dimensional combination.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">1.6</div>
<div>
<h3>Error in Measurement / मापन में त्रुटि</h3>
<p>Accuracy, precision, least count, random/systematic errors और error combination.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="two-lang">
<div>
<h4>Accuracy</h4>
<p>Closeness of measured value to the true value. अधिक accuracy का अर्थ true value के अधिक पास result.</p>
</div>
<div>
<h4>Precision</h4>
<p>Repeated measurements के बीच agreement. High precision का मतलब readings एक-दूसरे के बहुत close हैं।</p>
</div>
</div>

<h4>Types of Errors</h4>
<div class="grid-3">
<div class="info-box"><strong>Random</strong><span>अनियमित error; repeated observations से reduce हो सकती है।</span></div>
<div class="info-box"><strong>Systematic</strong><span>एक निश्चित pattern में error; instrument/calibration से जुड़ी हो सकती है।</span></div>
<div class="info-box"><strong>Gross</strong><span>Human mistakes जैसे wrong reading या wrong recording.</span></div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
Absolute Error = |Measured value − True/Mean value|<br>
Relative Error = Absolute Error / Mean value<br>
Percentage Error = Relative Error × 100
</div>

<h4>Combination of Errors</h4>
<div class="formula">
For addition/subtraction:<br>
If Z = A ± B, then ΔZ = ΔA + ΔB<br><br>
For multiplication/division:<br>
If Z = AB or A/B,<br>
ΔZ/Z = ΔA/A + ΔB/B<br><br>
For powers:<br>
If Z = Aⁿ,<br>
ΔZ/Z = n(ΔA/A)
</div>

<h4>Significant Figures</h4>
<ul>
<li>All non-zero digits are significant.</li>
<li>Zeros between non-zero digits are significant.</li>
<li>Leading zeros are generally not significant.</li>
<li>Trailing zeros after decimal are significant when written intentionally.</li>
<li>Rounding should follow the required precision of the calculation.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Unit 1 Quick Revision / त्वरित पुनरावृत्ति</h3>
<ul>
<li>SI is the standard system used in engineering.</li>
<li>Dimension of force = [M L T⁻²].</li>
<li>Dimension of work = [M L² T⁻²].</li>
<li>Dimension of power = [M L² T⁻³].</li>
<li>Homogeneous equation has same dimensions on both sides.</li>
<li>Accuracy and precision are different concepts.</li>
<li>Percentage error = relative error × 100.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>

