<p>Applications: lawn roller, inclined plane, pulling a load using an inclined force, structural force analysis.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">2.4</div>
<div>
<h3>Force, Momentum and Conservation of Linear Momentum</h3>
<p>Force motion change करता है; momentum moving body की quantity of motion को represent करता है।</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
Momentum: p = mv<br>
Force: F = dp/dt<br>
For constant mass: F = ma
</div>

<h4>Law of Conservation of Linear Momentum</h4>
<p>यदि system पर external resultant force zero है, तो total linear momentum constant रहता है।</p>

<div class="formula">
Before collision:<br>
Total momentum = m₁u₁ + m₂u₂<br><br>
After collision:<br>
Total momentum = m₁v₁ + m₂v₂<br><br>
Therefore:<br>
m₁u₁ + m₂u₂ = m₁v₁ + m₂v₂
</div>

<h4>Applications</h4>
<ul>
<li>Recoil of gun</li>
<li>Rocket propulsion</li>
<li>Collision of bodies</li>
<li>Jet propulsion</li>
<li>Explosive separation problems</li>
</ul>

<div class="diagram">
<div class="diagram-title">Recoil / Momentum Concept</div>
<div class="motion-box">
<div class="motion-ground"></div>
<div class="motion-ball"></div>
<div class="motion-arrow"></div>
</div>
<p class="small">Animation illustrates equal-and-opposite motion concept. Actual recoil depends on mass and momentum conditions.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">2.5</div>
<div>
<h3>Impulse and Applications</h3>
<p>Short time में large force का effect impulse से describe किया जाता है।</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
Impulse J = F Δt = Δp
</div>

<p>जब force बहुत कम समय के लिए लगता है, तब impulse momentum change के बराबर होता है।</p>
<ul>
<li>Hammer striking a nail</li>
<li>Cricket ball catching</li>
<li>Airbags in vehicles</li>
<li>Safety helmets</li>
<li>Collision protection systems</li>
</ul>
<p>Catch करते समय hands पीछे ले जाने से collision time बढ़ता है, इसलिए average force कम हो सकता है।</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">2.6</div>
<div>
<h3>Circular Motion</h3>
<p>Uniform और non-uniform circular motion, angular displacement, velocity, acceleration, frequency और time period.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<tr><th>Quantity</th><th>Meaning</th><th>SI Unit</th></tr>
<tr><td>Angular displacement θ</td><td>Angular change</td><td>radian</td></tr>
<tr><td>Angular velocity ω</td><td>Rate of angular displacement</td><td>rad/s</td></tr>
<tr><td>Angular acceleration α</td><td>Rate of change of angular velocity</td><td>rad/s²</td></tr>
<tr><td>Frequency f</td><td>Revolutions per second</td><td>Hz</td></tr>
<tr><td>Time period T</td><td>Time for one revolution</td><td>s</td></tr>
</table>
</div>

<div class="formula">
ω = θ/t<br>
ω = 2π/T = 2πf<br>
v = rω<br>
aₜ = rα<br>
a_c = v²/r = rω²
</div>

