     UNIT 3
========================================================= -->
<section class="section alt topic" id="unit3">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-title">
<div class="eyebrow">Unit 3 · 8 Periods</div>
<h2>Work, Power and Energy / कार्य, शक्ति एवं ऊर्जा</h2>
<p>Work, friction, kinetic energy, potential energy, conservation and power.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">3.1</div>
<div>
<h3>Work / कार्य</h3>
<p>Force के कारण displacement होने पर work done होता है।</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
W = F s cosθ
</div>

<div class="grid-3">
<div class="info-box"><strong>Positive</strong><span>Force और displacement same direction में हों; W &gt; 0.</span></div>
<div class="info-box"><strong>Zero</strong><span>Displacement zero या force perpendicular to displacement; W = 0.</span></div>
<div class="info-box"><strong>Negative</strong><span>Force displacement के opposite हो; W &lt; 0.</span></div>
</div>

<p><b>Examples:</b> gravitational force द्वारा upward lifting में gravity का work negative हो सकता है; circular motion में centripetal force instantaneous displacement के perpendicular होने के कारण zero work करता है।</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">3.2</div>
<div>
<h3>Friction / घर्षण</h3>
<p>Contact surfaces के relative motion या motion tendency का विरोध करने वाला force.</p>
</div>
</div>

<h4>Modern Concept</h4>
<p>Friction microscopic surface irregularities और adhesive interactions सहित कई effects के कारण होता है।</p>

<h4>Types</h4>
<ul>
<li>Static friction</li>
<li>Limiting friction</li>
<li>Kinetic / sliding friction</li>
<li>Rolling friction</li>
<li>Fluid friction</li>
</ul>

<div class="formula">
Limiting friction: F_lim = μN<br>
μ = F_lim/N
</div>

<h4>Reducing Friction</h4>
<ul>
<li>Lubrication</li>
<li>Ball/roller bearings</li>
<li>Polishing appropriate surfaces</li>
<li>Streamlined shapes in fluid motion</li>
</ul>

<h4>Engineering Applications</h4>
<p>Brakes, clutches, belt drives, bearings, walking, vehicle traction, machine components.</p>

