</svg>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">4.3</div>
<div>
<h3>Angular Momentum</h3>
<p>Rotational motion का momentum angular momentum कहलाता है।</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
L = Iω<br>
For particle: L = r × p
</div>

<h4>Conservation of Angular Momentum</h4>
<p>External torque zero होने पर angular momentum constant रहता है।</p>

<div class="formula">
I₁ω₁ = I₂ω₂
</div>

<p>Example: rotating skater arms अंदर करता है, moment of inertia घटता है और angular speed बढ़ती है, यदि external torque negligible हो।</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">4.4</div>
<div>
<h3>Moment of Inertia and Radius of Gyration</h3>
<p>Rotational motion में mass distribution का effect moment of inertia से represent होता है।</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
I = Σmr²<br>
I = Mk²<br>
k = √(I/M)
</div>

<h4>Physical Significance</h4>
<p>Mass axis से जितना दूर distributed होगा, moment of inertia उतना अधिक होगा। इसलिए same mass और same geometry नहीं होने पर rotational response बदल सकता है।</p>

<h4>Parallel Axis Theorem</h4>
<div class="formula">
I = I_G + Md²
</div>

<h4>Perpendicular Axis Theorem</h4>
<div class="formula">
I_z = I_x + I_y
</div>

<h4>Important Formulae</h4>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<tr><th>Body</th><th>Moment of Inertia</th></tr>
<tr><td>Thin rod about centre, perpendicular to length</td><td>I = ML²/12</td></tr>
<tr><td>Thin rod about end</td><td>I = ML²/3</td></tr>
<tr><td>Disc about central axis</td><td>I = MR²/2</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ring about central axis</td><td>I = MR²</td></tr>
<tr><td>Solid sphere about diameter</td><td>I = 2MR²/5</td></tr>
<tr><td>Hollow sphere about diameter</td><td>I = 2MR²/3</td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">4.5</div>
<div>
<h3>Rotational Kinetic Energy and Rolling</h3>
<p>Rotating body की kinetic energy और slant plane पर rolling.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
Rotational K.E. = 1/2 Iω²
</div>

<p>Rolling body में translational और rotational kinetic energy दोनों हो सकती हैं।</p>

<div class="formula">
Total K.E. = 1/2 Mv² + 1/2 Iω²
</div>

<p>Pure rolling के लिए:</p>
<div class="formula">v = Rω</div>

<div class="note">Rolling without slipping में point of contact की instantaneous velocity relative to surface zero होती है।</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">4.6</div>
<div>
<h3>Comparison: Linear vs Rotational Motion</h3>
<p>Equivalent physical quantities को याद करने की useful table.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<tr><th>Linear</th><th>Rotational</th></tr>
<tr><td>Displacement s</td><td>Angular displacement θ</td></tr>
<tr><td>Velocity v</td><td>Angular velocity ω</td></tr>
<tr><td>Acceleration a</td><td>Angular acceleration α</td></tr>
<tr><td>Mass m</td><td>Moment of inertia I</td></tr>
<tr><td>Force F</td><td>Torque τ</td></tr>
<tr><td>Momentum p = mv</td><td>Angular momentum L = Iω</td></tr>
<tr><td>K.E. = 1/2 mv²</td><td>K.E. = 1/2 Iω²</td></tr>
</table>
</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Unit 4 Formula Sheet</h3>
<div class="formula">
τ = rF sinθ<br>
L = Iω<br>
I = Mk²<br>
I = Σmr²<br>
I = I_G + Md²<br>
I_z = I_x + I_y<br>
Rotational K.E. = 1/2 Iω²<br>
v = Rω  [pure rolling]
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<!-- =========================================================
     UNIT 5
========================================================= -->
<section class="section alt topic" id="unit5">
<div class="container">
<div class="section-title">
<div class="eyebrow">Unit 5 · 12 Periods</div>
<h2>Properties of Matter / पदार्थ के गुण</h2>
<p>Elasticity, pressure, surface tension, viscosity, fluid motion, continuity and Bernoulli concept.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">5.1</div>
<div>
<h3>Elasticity, Stress, Strain and Modulus</h3>
<p>External force हटाने के बाद body के original shape में लौटने की tendency को elasticity कहते हैं।</p>
</div>
</div>

<h4>Stress</h4>
<div class="formula">Stress = Force / Area = F/A</div>

<h4>Strain</h4>
<div class="formula">Strain = Change in dimension / Original dimension</div>

<h4>Types of Stress</h4>
<ul>
<li>Longitudinal tensile stress</li>
<li>Longitudinal compressive stress</li>
<li>Shearing stress</li>
<li>Volumetric stress</li>
</ul>

<h4>Moduli of Elasticity</h4>
<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<tr><th>Modulus</th><th>Definition / Formula</th></tr>
<tr><td>Young's modulus Y</td><td>Longitudinal stress / longitudinal strain</td></tr>
<tr><td>Bulk modulus K</td><td>Volumetric stress / volumetric strain (with sign convention)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Modulus of rigidity G</td><td>Shearing stress / shearing strain</td></tr>
</table>
</div>

<h4>Hooke's Law</h4>
<div class="formula">Within elastic limit: Stress ∝ Strain</div>

