</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">5.5</div>
<div>
<h3>Fluid Motion, Streamline, Turbulent Flow and Reynolds Number</h3>
<p>Fluid के motion pattern को streamline और turbulent flow से describe किया जाता है।</p>
</div>
</div>

<h4>Streamline Flow</h4>
<p>Fluid particles smooth and ordered paths follow करते हैं; layers में relatively regular motion होता है।</p>

<h4>Turbulent Flow</h4>
<p>Irregular eddies और fluctuations वाला flow turbulent कहलाता है।</p>

<h4>Reynolds Number</h4>
<div class="formula">
Re = ρvD/η
</div>

<p>यह dimensionless number inertial effects और viscous effects के relative importance को compare करने में useful है। Pipe flow में lower Re generally laminar tendency और higher Re turbulent tendency indicate कर सकता है; exact transition depends on system conditions.</p>

<h4>Equation of Continuity</h4>
<div class="formula">
A₁v₁ = A₂v₂  [incompressible steady flow]
</div>

<h4>Bernoulli's Theorem</h4>
<div class="formula">
P + 1/2 ρv² + ρgh = constant
</div>

<p>Applications: Venturi meter, flow measurement, nozzles, fluid systems and energy analysis of ideal flow.</p>

