<h4>Reducing Heat Losses</h4>
<ul>
<li>Use thermal insulation.</li>
<li>Reduce unnecessary conduction paths.</li>
<li>Use suitable reflective surfaces against radiation.</li>
<li>Control convection using insulation and enclosure.</li>
</ul>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">6.3</div>
<div>
<h3>Temperature Scales and Specific Heat</h3>
<p>Celsius, Fahrenheit और Kelvin scales का relationship.</p>
</div>
</div>

<div class="formula">
C/5 = (F − 32)/9 = (K − 273.15)/5
</div>

<div class="table-wrap">
<table>
<tr><th>Scale</th><th>Common Reference</th><th>SI status</th></tr>
<tr><td>Celsius °C</td><td>Common engineering/education scale</td><td>Not SI base unit</td></tr>
<tr><td>Fahrenheit °F</td><td>Used in some countries/applications</td><td>Not SI</td></tr>
<tr><td>Kelvin K</td><td>Absolute thermodynamic temperature scale</td><td>SI base unit</td></tr>
</table>
</div>

<h4>Specific Heat Capacity</h4>
<div class="formula">
Q = mcΔT
</div>

<p>Specific heat capacity c वह heat है जो unit mass के temperature को unit degree बढ़ाने के लिए required होती है, given conditions में।</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<div class="topic-header">
<div class="topic-number">6.4</div>
<div>
<h3>Expansion of Solids, Liquids and Gases</h3>
<p>Temperature change के कारण dimensions/volume में change.</p>
</div>
</div>

<h4>Coefficients</h4>
<div class="formula">
Linear expansion: ΔL = αLΔT<br>
Surface expansion: ΔA = βAΔT<br>
Cubical expansion: ΔV = γVΔT
</div>

<h4>For isotropic solids</h4>
<div class="formula">
β ≈ 2α<br>
γ ≈ 3α
</div>

<p>Engineering applications: expansion joints, railway tracks, bridges, pipelines, bimetallic strips और machine design.</p>

