</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Unit 6 Quick Revision</h3>
<ul>
<li>Heat is transferred energy due to temperature difference.</li>
<li>Temperature SI unit is kelvin.</li>
<li>Heat transfer modes: conduction, convection, radiation.</li>
<li>Q = mcΔT for sensible heating under simple conditions.</li>
<li>ΔL = αLΔT.</li>
<li>For isotropic solids β ≈ 2α and γ ≈ 3α.</li>
<li>Thermal conductivity determines conductive heat transfer ability.</li>
<li>Mercury and bimetallic thermometers use thermal expansion principles in different ways.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</section>

