<h2>Selected Numericals / चुनिंदा संख्यात्मक प्रश्न</h2>
<p>Formula application की practice के लिए solved examples.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 1 — Velocity Dimensions</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> Find the dimensional formula of velocity.</p>
<p><b>Solution:</b> Velocity = displacement/time.</p>
<div class="formula">[v] = [L]/[T] = [L T⁻¹]</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> [L T⁻¹]</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 2 — Force</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> A 5 kg mass accelerates at 3 m/s². Find force.</p>
<div class="formula">F = ma = 5 × 3 = 15 N</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 15 N.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 3 — Momentum</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> A 2 kg body moves at 8 m/s. Find momentum.</p>
<div class="formula">p = mv = 2 × 8 = 16 kg·m/s</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 16 kg·m/s.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 4 — Kinetic Energy</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> Find kinetic energy of a 4 kg body moving at 5 m/s.</p>
<div class="formula">K.E. = 1/2 mv² = 1/2 × 4 × 25 = 50 J</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 50 J.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 5 — Power</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> A machine does 1200 J work in 20 s. Find power.</p>
<div class="formula">P = W/t = 1200/20 = 60 W</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 60 W.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 6 — Torque</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> A perpendicular force of 50 N acts at 0.4 m from pivot. Find torque.</p>
<div class="formula">τ = rF = 0.4 × 50 = 20 N·m</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 20 N·m.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 7 — Pressure</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> A force of 200 N acts over area 0.5 m². Find pressure.</p>
<div class="formula">P = F/A = 200/0.5 = 400 Pa</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 400 Pa.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 8 — Heat</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> A 2 kg material of specific heat 500 J/kg·K is heated through 10 K. Find heat supplied.</p>
<div class="formula">Q = mcΔT = 2 × 500 × 10 = 10000 J</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 10,000 J.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 9 — Temperature Conversion</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> Convert 40°C to Fahrenheit and Kelvin.</p>
<div class="formula">
F = 9/5 × 40 + 32 = 104°F<br>
K = 40 + 273.15 = 313.15 K
</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 104°F and 313.15 K.</p>
</div>

<div class="card">
<h3>Numerical 10 — Hooke's Law</h3>
<p><b>Question:</b> A spring extends 0.02 m under 4 N force. Find spring constant.</p>
<div class="formula">k = F/x = 4/0.02 = 200 N/m</div>
<p><b>Answer:</b> 200 N/m.</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>

